.TH PLAYPORT 1 "2025" "1.1.1" "PlayPort Manual"
.SH NAME
playport \- wireless virtual gamepad server for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playport
[\fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PlayPort creates a virtual uinput gamepad device on Linux and streams
input from the PlayPort Android client over your local network.
The Android app auto-discovers the server via UDP broadcast.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PORT
TCP port to listen on for input events. Defaults to \fB8007\fR.
.SH SETUP
The uinput kernel module must be loaded before running playport:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo modprobe uinput
.RE
.fi
.PP
Verify the device exists:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ls /dev/uinput
.RE
.fi
.SH PORTS
.TP
.B 8005/UDP
LAN server discovery broadcast
.TP
.B 8007/TCP
Input event stream (default)
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with default port:
.PP
.nf
.RS
playport
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run on a custom port:
.PP
.nf
.RS
playport 9000
.RE
.fi
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/tygrisiq/PlayPort/issues
.SH AUTHOR
Youssif Al-Halawche <yhalawche@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR evtest (1),
